            <ArticleTitle>[Equivalent occlusion of the left main coronary artery--case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>116-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the paper two cases are described of patients in whom during angiography coexistent occlusion of the left descending artery and left circumflex artery was found. ECG and echocardiography in both cases were not indicating such a high coronary vessel defect. In both patients angiography was performed leading in one case to development of shock with fatal outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
